WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:15.474
Brad: Be careful, be careful!

2
00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:17.005
Danny: What's the matter?

3
00:00:17.006 --> 00:00:20.737
Brad: You might be stepping on someone!

4
00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:22.578
Danny: What's that?

5
00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:25.577
Brad: It used to be the shrink-gun.

6
00:00:25.578 --> 00:00:27.680
Danny: Uh-oh.

7
00:00:27.681 --> 00:00:32.044
Brad: Yeah, it looks like it's broken.

8
00:00:32.045 --> 00:00:33.831
Danny: Can you fix it?

9
00:00:33.832 --> 00:00:36.692
Brad: I don't know. It will be tough.

10
00:00:36.693 --> 00:00:40.135
Danny: Oh, well. I guess we should give up.

11
00:00:40.136 --> 00:00:44.354
Brad: No. Let's see what we can find to fix it.

12
00:00:44.355 --> 00:00:46.727
Danny: Fine.

13
00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:48.497
Brad: Here's some old gum.

14
00:00:48.498 --> 00:00:49.989
Danny: Gross!

15
00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.834
Brad: It will help hold the pieces together.

16
00:00:53.835 --> 00:00:56.043
Danny: How about this rubber band?

17
00:00:56.044 --> 00:00:57.665
Brad: That will be good.

18
00:00:57.666 --> 00:01:00.334
We need something more.

19
00:01:00.335 --> 00:01:03.600
Danny: I found some string and a popsicle stick.

20
00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.484
Will that help?

21
00:01:05.485 --> 00:01:15.139
Brad: Sure. It's worth a try. Ta-da!

22
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.608
Danny: I don't think it's going to work.

23
00:01:17.609 --> 00:01:19.149
Brad: Don't say that.

24
00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.574
I haven't tried it yet.

25
00:01:21.575 --> 00:01:25.214
Danny: Okay. Give it a try.

26
00:01:25.215 --> 00:01:30.435
Brad: I think the bullies were standing here.

27
00:01:30.436 --> 00:01:32.675
Danny: Nothing is happening.

28
00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:34.458
Brad: I see that.

29
00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:36.649
Danny: Brad, we're both wet.

30
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.206
We don't have any more nano-putty.

31
00:01:39.207 --> 00:01:42.229
Danny: There's nothing more we can do!

32
00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:46.975
Brad: Maybe, if I had a paper clip or something metallic . . .

33
00:01:46.976 --> 00:01:50.709
Danny: Don't you ever give up?

34
00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.684
Brad: I see a gum wrapper.

35
00:01:53.685 --> 00:01:55.889
This could work.

36
00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:01.273
Danny: Let's go home!

37
00:02:01.274 --> 00:02:02.749
Brad: We can't go.

38
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.879
Brad: You agreed we would restore Chuck and Dave to normal size.

39
00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.583
Danny: I guess so.

40
00:02:08.584 --> 00:02:15.773
Brad: Good. Now, I just have to add this silver wrapper.

41
00:02:15.774 --> 00:02:17.819
Danny: Use your imagination.

42
00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.019
That's what works for me.

43
00:02:20.021 --> 00:02:27.713
Brad: Good idea. Big, big, big.

44
00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.785
Danny: I guess your imagination isn't very good.

45
00:02:31.786 --> 00:02:34.720
Brad: It appears that it isn't.

46
00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:38.762
Danny: Now do you agree that there's nothing we can do?

47
00:02:38.763 --> 00:02:42.240
Brad: No. You just told me what will make it work.

48
00:02:42.241 --> 00:02:43.684
Danny: What?

49
00:02:43.685 --> 00:02:47.782
Brad: Your imagination!
